# Both image builds use the REPO ROOT as their context (uv.lock describes the whole
# workspace), so without this every build uploads the git history and both dependency
# trees to the daemon.
#
# Two entries here are correctness rather than speed, and both only bite on a developer's
# machine — CI checks out clean, so a green CI run does not prove their absence is safe:
#
#   node_modules  — `web/Dockerfile` runs `npm ci` and then copies `web/`, so a host
#                   node_modules would overwrite the container's freshly-installed linux
#                   tree with the host's platform-specific binaries. The build then either
#                   fails confusingly or succeeds against a dependency set that is not the
#                   lockfile, quietly voiding the guarantee `npm ci` exists to give.
#   .env*         — Vite reads `.env` and `.env.local` at build time, so a developer with
#                   `VITE_API_BASE_URL` set locally would bake an API origin into the
#                   bundle. That is precisely what the runtime `config.js` exists to
#                   prevent, and the smoke test cannot see it, because the runtime value
#                   wins at call time and masks the compiled-in one.

.git
.github
.gitignore

# Python
.venv
venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/*.egg-info

# Node / web
**/node_modules
web/dist
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Environment — never let a local value reach a build.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Zimmer runtime state, never source.
.claude
.mcp.json
.npm-cache
**/*_stderr.log

# Docs and editor noise: nothing in either image reads them.
*.md
.idea
.vscode
.DS_Store
